Package: anydmx
Version: @VERSION@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Marian Raynov <marian.raynov@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/msvdm/AnyDMX
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), libegl1, libgl1, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libxcb-cursor0,
 libxcb-icccm4, libxcb-keysyms1, libxcb-shape0, libxcb-xinerama0,
 libfontconfig1, libfreetype6, libdbus-1-3
Recommends: network-manager
Description: Art-Net to DMX512 bridge for USB dongles
 AnyDMX captures Art-Net sent by any lighting application on this PC and
 re-emits it as DMX512 out a USB-RS485 dongle, replacing a chain of loopback
 adapter plus third-party bridge with a single window.
 .
 It shows what it is actually receiving — which universes are on the wire,
 from which source, at what rate — because when the rig is dark the first
 question is never whether the bridge is configured right, it is whether the
 console is sending anything at all.
 .
 Capturing Art-Net and driving DMX need no special privileges. Creating the
 dedicated lighting interface asks NetworkManager, which raises its own
 password prompt at the moment it is applied.
